# Wave W17-N (Mt. Smokestack): camp post — an ash researchers’ logger post beside their camp: a sturdy post with the white log sheet nailed to it where the fall gets recorded, a small gauge jar at its foot, on smoke turf (fully opaque, ground baked in). The design stands the researchers’ camp by the summit road, logging every fall; the posts carry the record. Split from Route 111’s dune post by the log sheet (a working post, not a marker).
